Ayodhyā has been considered as a sacred place by the Jains also. Several Tīrthaṅkaras had lived here.
The modern town of अयोध्या, on the bank of the river सरयू (also called Ghogrā), is about 130 kms. from Lucknow and 190 kms. from वाराणसी. It is in the Faizabad district of Uttar Pradesh. Apart from the spot said to be the birth-place of राम, the other places of interest for the tourists and the pilgrims are: Lakṣman Ghāṭ, स्वर्ग Dvār, हनुमान् Garhī, Kanak Bhavan and तुलसी Cowrā.
